  "result": "All 5 tests pass (the 3 prior tests plus the 2 new ones in tests/test_t2.py).\n\n**What I changed**\n\n- `netgraph/graph.py`: added three methods to `Graph`, which uses adjacency sets.\n  - `remove_edge(u, v)` discards the edge from both endpoints' sets, decrements the edge counter, and returns whether an edge was actually removed. Self-loops work because both discards hit the same set.\n  - `degree(u)` returns the size of the node's neighbour set, so a self-loop naturally counts once.\n  - `connected_components()` runs a BFS from each unseen node in ascending order. Each component is sorted before being appended, and the ascending start order guarantees components are ordered by smallest node.\n- `SPEC.md`: added the three new signatures to the public interface listing so the spec stays in sync with the code.\n\nAll three methods use the existing `_check` helper, so out-of-range node ids raise `IndexError` as the spec requires. No files under `tests/` were modified.",
